/-!
# Lemma A.1 (`lem:bad-link-generators`): the good link of a bad vertex

Formalized by Claude Sonnet 5.5.
Paper: Lemma A.1
(`lem:bad-link-generators`), with the setup of Appendix A.2.

> **Lemma A.1.** For a bad primitive vector `b`, the good link `L_b = lk_X(b^±) ∩ Y` is connected
> and `H₁(L_b; ℚ) = 0`.  Its second homology is generated by the tetrahedral boundaries
> `∂[u_k, u_{k+1}, v_l, v_{l+1}]` over base edges, and by the prism boundaries joining `θ_{k,l}` to
> `θ_{k+1,l}` or to `θ_{k,l+1}` over augmented base triangles.

## Dictionary: the paper's objects in the library's vocabulary

* **`X`, `Y`, `L_b`.**  `X` is `TernaryPoly.AugmentedFrameComplex.ambient`, whose faces are the
  nonempty subsets of the four lines `augmentedLine g 0..3` of an integral basis `g`
  (`augmentedLine g i` is the line spanned by `g·e_i`, `i < 3`, resp. by `g(e₀+e₁)` for `i = 3`);
  `Y` is the full subcomplex on the Good lines (`ModThreeGoodAction.Good`: the line contains an
  integral vector with coordinate sum nonzero modulo three).  For a bad line `b`, `badLink b` is
  `GoodLinkExtraction.augmentedGoodLink {b} = goodLink ambient Good {b}`: its faces are the nonempty
  finite sets `s` of Good lines with `{b} ∪ s ∈ ambient`.  It is literally the simplicial complex
  `L_b`; it has vertices (`n = 1`), edges (`n = 2`) and triangles (`n = 3`), and no higher faces
  (`bad_link_no_tetrahedra`).
* **Chains and homology.**  `OrientedListChains.chains C n` is the `ℚ`-span of the oriented simplices
  `simplex [a₁,…,a_n]` (alternating, hence zero on repeated vertices) with `n` vertices,
  `OrientedListChains.boundary` is the alternating boundary, extended to the augmentation
  (`boundary (simplex [a]) = simplex []`).  Hence `chains (badLink b) 1` are the `0`-chains,
  `chains (badLink b) 2` the `1`-chains, `chains (badLink b) 3` the `2`-chains of `L_b`, and:
  * "`L_b` is connected" is nonemptiness (`bad_link_nonempty`) together with `H̃₀(L_b; ℚ) = 0`: every
    augmentation-zero vertex combination is the boundary of an edge combination in `L_b`
    (`bad_link_connected`), and, in graph form, any two vertices are joined by a path of edges
    (`bad_link_graph_connected`);
  * `H₁(L_b; ℚ) = 0`: every `1`-cycle in `chains (badLink b) 2` is the boundary of a `2`-chain of
    `L_b` (`bad_link_H1_zero`);
  * since `L_b` has no `3`-simplices, `H₂(L_b; ℚ)` is the space of cycles in `chains (badLink b) 3`;
    "generated by" means that every such cycle lies in the `ℚ`-span of the two sphere families
    (`bad_link_H2_generated`), and all generators are cycles of `L_b`
    (`bad_link_generators_cycles`).
* **Fibres `u_k`, bases `(b, X, Y)`.**  Every bad line is `augmentedLine g 0` for an integral basis
  `g` (`RationalLineBasis.rationalLine_eq_augmentedLine`), the other columns being `X` and `Y`.
  For such a basis, `xFiber g k = ⟨X + k b⟩`, `yFiber g l = ⟨Y + l b⟩`, `zFiber g m = ⟨X + Y + m b⟩`
  (`CoherentPrismReduction.fiberLine g i k`, the line spanned by the vector with coordinates
  `(k,1,0)`, `(k,0,1)`, `(k,1,1)` in the basis `g`).  The base vertices of `Z` are the images
  `⟨X⟩, ⟨Y⟩, ⟨X+Y⟩` in `(ℤ³/ℤb)`, the lifts `u_k = u_0 + k b` of `u = ⟨X⟩` form the path `P_u`.
* **Tetrahedral spheres.**  `tetraSphere g k l = ∂[u_k, u_{k+1}, v_l, v_{l+1}]` with `u_k = xFiber g k`
  and `v_l = yFiber g l`; `tetraSpheres b` collects them over all bases `g = (b, X, Y)` with
  `⟨X⟩, ⟨Y⟩` Good, i.e. over all base edges of `Z` (and all `k, l`).
* **Prism spheres.**  For a basis with `⟨X⟩, ⟨Y⟩, ⟨X+Y⟩` Good (an augmented base triangle), the
  triangles `θ_{k,l} = [xFiber g k, yFiber g l, zFiber g (k+l)]` (`CoherentPrismReduction.coherent`)
  are the `2`-simplices of `L_b` over the triangle, and `AugmentedPrismCaps.prismSphere g` is
  the boundary of the two augmented tetrahedra `[X,Y,Z,X'] + [Y,Z,X',Z']` (`Z = X+Y`, `X' = X+b`,
  `Z' = Z+b`) of the paper's equation `eq:prism-cap`.  It is `θ_{1,0} - θ_{0,0}` plus the four
  side faces; for the basis `affineBasis g (k,l)` this is the prism joining `θ_{k,l}` to
  `θ_{k+1,l}` (`prismSphere_affineBasis_eq`) and for `affineBasis (g * swapGL) (l,k)` (the basis
  with `X` and `Y` exchanged) it is, up to sign, the prism joining `θ_{k,l}` to `θ_{k,l+1}`
  (`prismSphere_swap_eq`).  `prismSpheres b` collects `prismSphere g` over all bases with first line
  `b` and Good `⟨X⟩, ⟨Y⟩, ⟨X+Y⟩`; both kinds of prisms belong to it
  (`prismSphere_affineBasis_mem`, `prismSphere_swap_mem`), so no prism of the paper is missing.

## The statement in code (definitions in `Proofs/LiteralExports/AppendixALink/Defs.lean`)

```
abbrev badLink (b : RationalLine) := augmentedGoodLink {b}                      -- L_b
def tetraSphere (g : IntegralGL) (k l : ℤ) : Chain RationalLine :=
  boundary (simplex [xFiber g k, xFiber g (k+1), yFiber g l, yFiber g (l+1)])    -- ∂[u_k,u_{k+1},v_l,v_{l+1}]
def tetraSpheres (b : RationalLine) : Set (Chain RationalLine) :=
  {c | ∃ (g : IntegralGL) (k l : ℤ), augmentedLine g 0 = b ∧ Good (xFiber g 0).val ∧
      Good (yFiber g 0).val ∧ c = tetraSphere g k l}                              -- frame quantifier g = (b,X,Y)
def prismSpheres (b : RationalLine) : Set (Chain RationalLine) :=
  {c | ∃ g : IntegralGL, augmentedLine g 0 = b ∧ Good (xFiber g 0).val ∧
      Good (yFiber g 0).val ∧ Good (zFiber g 0).val ∧ c = AugmentedPrismCaps.prismSphere g}
```

The quantification "over base edges" (resp. "over augmented base triangles") is the quantification
over all integral bases `g = (b, X, Y)` with `⟨X⟩, ⟨Y⟩` (resp. also `⟨X+Y⟩`) Good together with
all `k, l`: the lines `u_k = ⟨X + k b⟩`, `v_l = ⟨Y + l b⟩` run over the fibres of the base edge
`(⟨X⟩,⟨Y⟩)` of `Z`, and the triangles `θ_{k,l}` over the fibres of the base triangle; the choice of
compatible representatives with `u_0 = u_1 + u_2` in the paper is the choice of the basis `g`.
Reindexing: the sphere of the basis `affineBasis g (k,l)` is the prism from `θ_{k,l}` to
`θ_{k+1,l}` (`prismSphere_affineBasis_eq`), that of `affineBasis (g * swapGL) (l,k)` the prism
from `θ_{k,l}` to `θ_{k,l+1}` (`prismSphere_swap_eq`).

## What is proved

All items are proved for every bad line `b` (`hb : ¬ Good b.val`), by the filtration of the
paper's proof carried out on chains: the projection `p : L_b → Z` (`BadVertexProjection.vertex`)
to the good rank-two complex `Z` with the descended residue functional `phi`, acyclicity of `Z`
(`RankTwoGoodFilling.good_exactness`), lifting of the fillings of `Z` to `L_b` (triangles lift to the
`θ_{k,l}`, edges to cross edges, vertices to fibre points), then exactness fibrewise: over a vertex by
the contractible path `P_u`, over an edge by the mixed triangles of the join `P_u * P_v`, over an
augmented triangle by the grid complex of the `θ_{k,l}` with the prism spheres as the relative
`3`-cells.  For the generation of `H₂` the cap decomposition of the library
(`BadVertexCoherentElimination.eliminate_coherent`, `BadVertexMixedFilling`) is rerun while keeping
track of the caps: their boundaries are prism spheres and tetrahedral spheres.
-/

noncomputable section

namespace TernaryPeriodPolynomials.Argument.Statements.AppendixALink

open TernaryPoly TernaryPoly.ModThreeGoodAction TernaryPoly.AugmentedFrameComplex
  TernaryPoly.OrientedListChains TernaryPoly.GoodLinkExtraction TernaryPoly.CoherentPrismReduction
  TernaryPeriodPolynomials.Argument.AppendixALink

/-- `L_b` is nonempty: it has a vertex. -/
theorem bad_link_nonempty (b : RationalLine) (hb : ¬Good b.val) :
    ∃ a : RationalLine, ({a} : Finset RationalLine) ∈ badLink b :=
  exists_vertex b hb

/-- **Lemma A.1, connectedness**: `H̃₀(L_b; ℚ) = 0`.  Every zero-chain of `L_b` of augmentation zero
(`boundary c = 0`) is the boundary of a one-chain of `L_b`. -/
theorem bad_link_connected (b : RationalLine) (hb : ¬Good b.val) {c : Chain RationalLine}
    (hc : c ∈ chains (badLink b) 1) (hd : boundary c = 0) :
    ∃ t ∈ chains (badLink b) 2, boundary t = c :=
  connected_link b hb hc hd

/-- **Lemma A.1, `H₁(L_b; ℚ) = 0`**: every one-cycle of `L_b` is the boundary of a two-chain of
`L_b`. -/
theorem bad_link_H1_zero (b : RationalLine) (hb : ¬Good b.val) {c : Chain RationalLine}
    (hc : c ∈ chains (badLink b) 2) (hd : boundary c = 0) :
    ∃ t ∈ chains (badLink b) 3, boundary t = c :=
  simply_connected_link b hb hc hd

/-- **Lemma A.1, connectedness (graph form)**: any two vertices of `L_b` are joined by a path of
edges of `L_b` (`Adjacent b x y`: `x ≠ y` and `{x,y}` is an edge of `badLink b`). -/
theorem bad_link_graph_connected (b : RationalLine) (hb : ¬Good b.val) (a a' : RationalLine)
    (ha : ({a} : Finset RationalLine) ∈ badLink b) (ha' : ({a'} : Finset RationalLine) ∈ badLink b) :
    Relation.ReflTransGen (Adjacent b) a a' :=
  graph_connected b hb a a' ha ha'

/-- `L_b` has no faces with four vertices, so `chains (badLink b) 4 = 0` and `H₂(L_b; ℚ)` is the
space of cycles in `chains (badLink b) 3`. -/
theorem bad_link_no_tetrahedra (b : RationalLine) (hb : ¬Good b.val) :
    chains (badLink b) 4 = ⊥ :=
  chains_four_eq_bot b hb

/-- **Lemma A.1, generation of `H₂`**: every two-cycle of `L_b` is a `ℚ`-linear combination of the
tetrahedral spheres `∂[u_k,u_{k+1},v_l,v_{l+1}]` and the prism spheres. -/
theorem bad_link_H2_generated (b : RationalLine) (hb : ¬Good b.val) {c : Chain RationalLine}
    (hc : c ∈ chains (badLink b) 3) (hd : boundary c = 0) :
    c ∈ Submodule.span ℚ (tetraSpheres b ∪ prismSpheres b) :=
  generation b hb hc hd

/-- Every tetrahedral and every prism sphere is a two-cycle of `L_b` (so the generators of
`bad_link_H2_generated` represent classes of `H₂(L_b; ℚ)`). -/
theorem bad_link_generators_cycles (b : RationalLine) (hb : ¬Good b.val) {c : Chain RationalLine}
    (hc : c ∈ tetraSpheres b ∪ prismSpheres b) :
    c ∈ chains (badLink b) 3 ∧ boundary c = 0 :=
  generator_mem b hb hc

/-- **Lemma A.1** (`lem:bad-link-generators`): all statements together. -/
theorem lemma_A1 (b : RationalLine) (hb : ¬Good b.val) :
    (∃ a : RationalLine, ({a} : Finset RationalLine) ∈ badLink b) ∧
    (∀ c ∈ chains (badLink b) 1, boundary c = 0 →
      ∃ t ∈ chains (badLink b) 2, boundary t = c) ∧
    (∀ c ∈ chains (badLink b) 2, boundary c = 0 →
      ∃ t ∈ chains (badLink b) 3, boundary t = c) ∧
    (∀ c ∈ chains (badLink b) 3, boundary c = 0 →
      c ∈ Submodule.span ℚ (tetraSpheres b ∪ prismSpheres b)) ∧
    (∀ c ∈ tetraSpheres b ∪ prismSpheres b, c ∈ chains (badLink b) 3 ∧ boundary c = 0) ∧
    chains (badLink b) 4 = ⊥ :=
  TernaryPeriodPolynomials.Argument.AppendixALink.lemma_A1 b hb

/-- Dictionary: the prism joining `θ_{k,l}` to `θ_{k+1,l}` is the prism sphere of the basis
`affineBasis g (k,l)`; its boundary is `θ_{k+1,l} - θ_{k,l}` minus the four side faces. -/
theorem prismSphere_affineBasis_eq (g : IntegralGL) (k l : ℤ) :
    AugmentedPrismCaps.prismSphere (affineBasis g (k,l)) =
      coherent g (k+1,l) - coherent g (k,l) - horizontalResidual g (k,l) :=
  TernaryPeriodPolynomials.Argument.AppendixALink.prismSphere_affineBasis_eq g k l

/-- Dictionary: the prism joining `θ_{k,l}` to `θ_{k,l+1}` is, up to sign, the prism sphere of the
basis with `X` and `Y` exchanged. -/
theorem prismSphere_swap_eq (g : IntegralGL) (k l : ℤ) :
    coherent g (k,l+1) - coherent g (k,l) =
      -AugmentedPrismCaps.prismSphere (affineBasis (g * swapGL) (l,k)) +
        verticalResidual g (k,l) :=
  TernaryPeriodPolynomials.Argument.AppendixALink.prismSphere_swap_eq g k l

/-- Both kinds of prism spheres of the paper belong to `prismSpheres b`. -/
theorem prismSphere_affineBasis_mem {b : RationalLine} (g : IntegralGL)
    (hgb : augmentedLine g 0 = b) (hbad : ¬Good b.val) (hx : Good (xFiber g 0).val)
    (hy : Good (yFiber g 0).val) (hz : Good (zFiber g 0).val) (p : ℤ × ℤ) :
    AugmentedPrismCaps.prismSphere (affineBasis g p) ∈ prismSpheres b :=
  TernaryPeriodPolynomials.Argument.AppendixALink.prismSphere_affineBasis_mem g hgb hbad hx hy hz p

theorem prismSphere_swap_mem {b : RationalLine} (g : IntegralGL)
    (hgb : augmentedLine g 0 = b) (hbad : ¬Good b.val) (hx : Good (xFiber g 0).val)
    (hy : Good (yFiber g 0).val) (hz : Good (zFiber g 0).val) (p : ℤ × ℤ) :
    AugmentedPrismCaps.prismSphere (affineBasis (g * swapGL) p) ∈ prismSpheres b :=
  TernaryPeriodPolynomials.Argument.AppendixALink.prismSphere_swap_mem g hgb hbad hx hy hz p

/-- The tetrahedral spheres of every base edge belong to `tetraSpheres b`. -/
theorem tetraSphere_mem {b : RationalLine} (g : IntegralGL) (hgb : augmentedLine g 0 = b)
    (hx : Good (xFiber g 0).val) (hy : Good (yFiber g 0).val) (k l : ℤ) :
    tetraSphere g k l ∈ tetraSpheres b :=
  ⟨g,k,l,hgb,hx,hy,rfl⟩

end TernaryPeriodPolynomials.Argument.Statements.AppendixALink
